!Name: slowfuseship
!C A growing spaceship with a slowly burning fuse at the back.
!C The front of the ship travels at c/2 creating lots of blinkers and a
!C few other stable objects on the edge.  A blinker-fuse burns the gliders
!C and stable objects back and forth from side to side, while advancing
!C forwards with a speed of 7c/46.  If more blinkers are added to make a
!C thicker trail (by any multiple of 3 blinkers), the blinker-fuse will
!C take longer to move from side to side, and so will advance slower.  The
!C resulting spaceship can have a back end which advances arbitrarily slowly.
!C David I. Bell, September 2006
!Source: jslife-oversize-20100113
